  <p>[ <a class="reference internal" href="../index.html#cli-aws"><span class="std std-ref">aws</span></a> . <a class="reference internal" href="index.html#cli-aws-dynamodb"><span class="std std-ref">dynamodb</span></a> ]</p>
<div class="section" id="get-item">
<span id="cli-aws-dynamodb-get-item"></span><h1>get-item<a class="headerlink" href="#get-item" title="Permalink to this heading">¶</a></h1>
<div class="section" id="description">
<h2>Description<a class="headerlink" href="#description" title="Permalink to this heading">¶</a></h2>
<p>The <code class="docutils literal notranslate"><span class="pre">GetItem</span></code> operation returns a set of attributes for the item with the given primary key. If there is no matching item, <code class="docutils literal notranslate"><span class="pre">GetItem</span></code> does not return any data and there will be no <code class="docutils literal notranslate"><span class="pre">Item</span></code> element in the response.</p>
<blockquote>
<div><code class="docutils literal notranslate"><span class="pre">GetItem</span></code> provides an eventually consistent read by default. If your application requires a strongly consistent read, set <code class="docutils literal notranslate"><span class="pre">ConsistentRead</span></code> to <code class="docutils literal notranslate"><span class="pre">true</span></code> . Although a strongly consistent read might take more time than an eventually consistent read, it always returns the last updated value.</div></blockquote>
<p>See also: <a class="reference external" href="https://docs.aws.amazon.com/goto/WebAPI/dynamodb-2012-08-10/GetItem">AWS API Documentation</a></p>
</div>
<div class="section" id="synopsis">
